 "A Blit from a screen camera's target: green 0x36 against the Editor's 0x37. The batch-mode Editor's screen is BGRA8Unorm without sRGB encoding and keeps the camera's linear 0.214 as 0x37; Unbound's stand-in is sRGB-encoded, where that value (encoded 127.5) is stored as 127 on Metal, presumably a tie (as the Editor's Metal device stores it, srgb.drawn.bytes). The windowed Editor's Game view is sRGB (BGRA8Unorm_sRGB) and reads 0x7f here (metal-windowed.jsonl)": [
  "screencamera.drawn.pixels"
 ],
 "ReadPixels of the screen in a screen camera's onPostRender: Unbound reads its stand-in's bytes, sRGB-encoded as its screen holds them (0x7f; the windowed Editor's Game view is sRGB too), the batch-mode Editor's screen is not encoded (0x37, the camera's linear 0.214)": [
  "screenself.read.pixels"
 ],
 "A screen camera's command buffer blitting CameraTarget onto itself through a shader: the batch-mode Editor's shader samples white (half of 1 everywhere), Unbound's samples the camera's image (a copy made before the draw); one measured case, the Editor's mechanism not established. Queued": [
  "screenself.blit.pixels"
 ],
